From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:45:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: edp: Program v8 TX resistor code offsets and lane
 settings

The v8 TX lane setup before PLL start programs the resistor codes but
not the resistor code offsets, and leaves two further lane registers at
0x88 and 0x90 untouched, so their values depend on what ran before.

Program RES_CODE_LANE_OFFSET_TX0/TX1 to 0x06 and the registers at 0x88
and 0x90 to 0x44 and 0x01 in both TX blocks. The values match what the
platform's firmware programs on the Surface Laptop 8, and they are part
of the sequence that trains that laptop's panel at 5.4 Gbps. Whether
each of them is required there has not been isolated. They have not
been checked on other Glymur boards, and the registers at 0x88 and 0x90
have no public name.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
index 98625c28ecb..1414d8993cb 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
@@ -84,6 +84,9 @@
 #define TXn_TRAN_DRVR_EMP_EN                    0x0078
 #define TXn_VMODE_CTRL1                         0x007c
 #define TXn_LDO_CONFIG                          0x0084
+/* v8 TX lane registers without a public name */
+#define TXn_V8_UNKNOWN_0088                     0x0088
+#define TXn_V8_UNKNOWN_0090                     0x0090
 #define TXn_DCC0_CTRL                           0x00c8
 #define TXn_DCC1_CTRL                           0x00d0
 #define TXn_DCC_DONE                            0x00e0
@@ -538,6 +541,10 @@ static void qcom_edp_configure_tx_pre_pll_v8_lane(void __iomem *tx, u32 interfac
 	writel(0x00, tx + TXn_SLEW_CNTL);
 	writel(0x60, tx + TXn_RES_CODE_LANE_TX);
 	writel(0x60, tx + TXn_RES_CODE_LANE_TX1);
+	writel(0x06, tx + TXn_RES_CODE_LANE_OFFSET_TX0);
+	writel(0x06, tx + TXn_RES_CODE_LANE_OFFSET_TX1);
+	writel(0x44, tx + TXn_V8_UNKNOWN_0088);
+	writel(0x01, tx + TXn_V8_UNKNOWN_0090);
 }
 
 static void qcom_edp_configure_lanes_after_pll_v8(const struct qcom_edp *edp)
